{"created": "2026-06-13T16:09:11.807354+00:00", "modified": "2026-06-14T11:11:53.193646+00:00", "id": 20681219, "conceptrecid": "20680952", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20681219", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.20680952", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20681219", "metadata": {"title": "Yang-Mills Amendments and Refinements", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20681219", "publication_date": "2026-06-13", "description": "<h3>Abstract</h3>\n<p>We present a parameter-free geometric framework unifying Conformal Cyclic Cosmology (CCC), Kaluza-Klein structures, and emergent Quantum Chromodynamics (QCD). By establishing a 5D Einstein-Kaluza-Klein (EKK Action) substrate over a compact circle <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> with a fixed macroscopic radius <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">&tau;</span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">7</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">&minus;1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">&nbsp;Mpc</span></span></span></span></span></span>, spatial Planckian boundaries are structurally mapped onto the essential spectrum of a torsion-twisted Dirac operator. We explicitly resolve the historical Light Scalar Glueball Paradox by reframing the universal <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">312.8</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">&nbsp;MeV</span></span></span></span></span></span> vacuum resonance floor as the intrinsic dynamic mass of the <strong>constituent gluon operator itself</strong> in the infrared (IR) limit. Bound states of multi-gluon trajectories (<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">g</span><span class=\"mbin\">&otimes;</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">g</span></span></span></span></span>) are shown to scale natively to the <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1.5</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">&ndash;</span></span><span class=\"mord\">1.7</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">&nbsp;GeV</span></span></span></span></span></span> meson sector, matching empirical Particle Data Group (PDG) candidates.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "brown (wylde), william", "affiliation": "independent", "orcid": "0009-0004-1762-5792"}], "keywords": ["Tau Universe Framework"], "resource_type": {"title": "Data paper", "type": "publication", "subtype": "datapaper"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "20680952"}}]}}, "title": "Yang-Mills Amendments and Refinements", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20681219", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20681219", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20681219?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20681219", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20681219", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.20681219", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20681219/draft/